# **Replace** (ADR-0403), the last of the three things milestone two said it
# left out and the one that needed the model to grow: an action of a person's
# that is more than one of ADR-0387's four operations.
#
# The claims, in the order the keys drive them:
#
#   - Ctrl-R asks twice, in the same framed box `Find` and `Open` use -- the
#     titles are `Replace` and `With`, and the first answer survives the
#     second being typed;
#   - matching is `Seek`'s, which is **case-insensitive** (6.1.3 folds an
#     identifier, so a person searching for `writeln` means `WriteLn` too),
#     and what goes in is the replacement exactly -- which is how one spelling
#     becomes another;
#   - every occurrence in the document goes, including two on one line, so
#     the scan does not stop at the first match of a line;
#   - **one Ctrl-Z reverses the whole action.** This is the claim the feature
#     was built around: three replacements are six entries in the journal, and
#     an undo that reversed one of the six would be an undo of nothing anybody
#     did. One Ctrl-Y puts them all back, which is the same group read the
#     other way;
#   - an empty answer to `With` is a **deletion** and not a refusal, that
#     being the commonest thing anyone does with this;
#   - and a pattern that matches nothing says so and changes nothing, as a
#     failed search does.
name r.pas
size 12 34
push writeln(one); WriteLn(two);
push   writeln(three)
push begin end
draw
ctrl R
keys writeln
draw
ctrl M
keys print
draw
ctrl M
draw
ctrl Z
draw
ctrl Y
draw
ctrl R
keys print
ctrl M
ctrl M
draw
ctrl R
keys nosuch
ctrl M
keys x
ctrl M
draw
